# An alternative cost a static ability gives some spells is judged on the spell the card would be on the stack, under its
# caster, with the continuous effects that would apply to it there (CR 601.2a-b, 601.3e, 118.9), not on the card where it
# is. Bot1 controls Dracogenesis ("You may cast Dragon spells without paying their mana costs") and Arcane Adaptation
# naming Dragon ("The same is true for creature spells you control"). Cruelclaw's Heist with its gift exiles Bot2's
# Gigantic Big Bear and lets Bot1 cast it. In Bot2's exile, owned by Bot2, the Bear is no Dragon; as Bot1's creature spell
# it is one (CR 611.3a), so Bot1 casts it without paying its mana cost - with three mana left, {5}{G}{G} could not be paid
# - and it enters a Dragon.

